<capabilities>
<p>The LC-100 carries fuel sufficient for more than a week of travel at 1G and food stores for a month of sustained space travel. Luxury quarters accommodate seven passengers, and a five-ton cargo bay handles personal freight. The Astrolux can land in the small craft bay of any DropShip or JumpShip as easily as at a planetary port, making it suitable for complex multi-leg voyages.</p>
</capabilities>

<overview>
<p>The Lockheed/CBM LC-100 Astrolux StarYacht is the most popular long-range civilian spacecraft designed for private ownership in the Inner Sphere. Produced at Lockheed/CBM's Donegal facilities, it has been the defining craft of its category since its introduction in 2953.</p>
</overview>

<history>
<p>Introduced in 2953, the Astrolux's combination of range, comfort, and versatility prompted numerous knock-off designs and legal disputes over the following century. Despite that competition, the LC-100 remains one of Lockheed/CBM's most successful civilian products.</p>
</history>

